--- a growing int handed to `fmt` chooses the form that keeps every digit
--- only where it is the value: a width past 64 bits beside a float had
--- chosen it, and the float reached the growing value's place — an
--- internal error in both modes (crow check --self). The width stops, as
--- an int of 64 bits does, in both modes

log[fmt[2 ^ 100, commas = true]]
log[fmt[2.5, decimals = 2]]
log[fmt[2.5, width = 2 ^ 100]]
